      "text": "IOT Database Technology differences:\r\nSr. No. Technology Best suited for\r\n1 SQL Structured and relational IoT data\r\n2 NoSQL Large, flexible, rapidly changing IoT data\r\n3 Time-Series Sensor data recorded over time\r\n4 Key-Value Very fast access to device data\r\n5 Graph Relationships between IoT devices and entities\r\n6 Cloud Scalable, remote, large-scale IoT data storage\r\nIOT \r\nDatabase \r\nTechnology\r\nDefinition Types / Examples IoT Use Applications\r\nRelational \r\nDatabases \r\n(SQL)\r\nDatabases that store \r\ndata in structured \r\ntables with rows \r\nand columns and \r\nuse SQL for \r\nquerying and \r\nmanaging data.\r\nMySQL, \r\nPostgreSQL, \r\nOracle, SQL \r\nServer\r\nStores structured \r\ninformation such as \r\ndevice details, \r\nusers, \r\nconfigurations, and \r\ntransactions.\r\nSmart homes, \r\nindustrial IoT, \r\nhealthcare \r\nsystems, device \r\nmanagement\r\nNoSQL \r\nDatabases\r\nDatabases designed \r\nto store large \r\namounts of \r\nunstructured or \r\nsemi-structured \r\ndata with flexible \r\nschemas.\r\nMongoDB \u2013\r\nDocument; \r\nCassandra \u2013\r\nWide-column; \r\nCouchDB \u2013\r\nDocument\r\nHandles large\r\nvolumes of rapidly \r\ngenerated sensor \r\nand device data.\r\nSmart cities, \r\nconnected \r\nvehicles, large \r\nsensor networks, \r\nIoT platforms\r\nTime-Series \r\nDatabases\r\nDatabases optimized \r\nfor data that is \r\ncollected and stored \r\naccording to time, \r\nsuch as continuous \r\nsensor \r\nmeasurements.\r\nInfluxDB, \r\nTimescaleDB, \r\nOpenTSDB\r\nStores temperature, \r\nhumidity, pressure, \r\nspeed, energy \r\nconsumption, and \r\nother time-stamped \r\nreadings.\r\nEnvironmental \r\nmonitoring, \r\nindustrial \r\nmonitoring, \r\npredictive \r\nmaintenance, \r\nenergy monitoring\r\nKey-Value \r\nDatabases\r\nDatabases that store \r\ninformation as key\ufffevalue pairs, \r\nallowing very fast \r\nretrieval using a \r\nunique key.\r\nRedis, Amazon \r\nDynamoDB, Riak\r\nStores device \r\nstatus, sensor \r\nvalues, session \r\ninformation, and \r\nfrequently accessed \r\nreal-time data.\r\nReal-time IoT\r\ndashboards, smart \r\nappliances, device \r\nstate management, \r\ncaching",
